    <Notes ShowOnLoad="0" Notes="TCE1:TCE-SC-20261014-R1&#10;Hardware: JPT YDFLP-E-60-M7-M-R 60 W, serial MC2BDJD71684; lens: F-Theta 174 mm; material: titanium (link the exact grade and batch in the experiment record).&#10;Titanium track-width/resolution proxy on JPT M7 60 W with F-Theta 174 mm. Ten groups have five parallel LightBurn Line strokes at centre-to-centre pitches 20/30/40/50/60/80/100/150/200/300 um. Fixed P20%, F48 kHz, V2000 mm/s, PW200 ns and one pass. Under a calibrated microscope, measure individual track width and note the smallest pitch at which adjacent tracks remain separated. This is a material/focus/threshold-dependent mark-width proxy, not the optical beam waist; exact spot diameter requires a beam profiler or a validated burn-threshold method.&#10;Canvas 76 x 45 mm; registered bounds 98 x 82.5 mm. First: full-area cross-hatched cleaning, 20% / 48 kHz / 2000 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.05 mm; second: black marker/label layer 25% / 60 kHz / 150 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.01 mm, one pass."/>
</LightBurnProject>
